<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 8 August, from 870 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/870">870 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,156 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Meerssen partitions Lotharingia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a> divided the lands of their late nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-ii">Lothair II</a> between West and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a>. The partition helped shape the later frontier between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1164">1164 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">862 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hassan II of Alamut proclaims the qiyama to the Nizari Ismailis</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At a public gathering at the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alamut">Alamut</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismailism">Nizari</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> Hassan II proclaimed the qiyama and announced that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> practice would change from traditional Islamic practice. In standard Islamic eschatology the qiyama comes at the end of time.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Isma'ilism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1220">1220 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">806 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Estonians defeat the Swedes at the Battle of Lihula</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonians">Estonians</a> defeated invading Swedes in a battle for control of the castle at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lihula">Lihula</a>, described in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-chronicle-of-henry">Chronicle of Henry of Livonia</a> and the Livonian Rhymed Chronicle. The exact date is uncertain, but some historians place it on 8 August.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonians">Estonians</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1264">1264 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">762 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mudéjar rebels take the Alcázar of Jerez de la Frontera</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Early in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudejar">Mudéjar</a> revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, the Muslim inhabitants of Jerez, aided by allies from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeciras">Algeciras</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarifa">Tarifa</a>, took the town's alcázar after its commander, Nuño González de Lara, deserted his post. Reinforcements from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> arrived two days too late.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudejar-revolt-of-1264-1266">Mudéjar revolt of 1264–1266</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tycho-brahe" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tycho-brahe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1576">1576 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">450 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Foundation stone is laid for Tycho Brahe's Uraniborg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Work began on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tycho-brahe">Tycho Brahe</a>'s observatory on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ven-island">Hven</a>, granted to him by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-of-denmark">Frederick II of Denmark</a>. Its precise naked-eye observations later allowed Kepler to derive his laws of planetary motion.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allied attack at Amiens breaks the German line</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British, Australian, Canadian and French troops, with hundreds of tanks, broke through near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amiens">Amiens</a>. Ludendorff called it the 'black day of the German army'; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a> Offensive had begun.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union declares war on Japan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and, within hours, launched a massive invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>. Coming between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atomic-bombings-of-hiroshima-and-nagasaki">atomic bombings</a>, it helped persuade Japan's leaders to surrender.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1974">1974 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard Nixon announces his resignation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a televised address, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-nixon">Richard Nixon</a> said he would resign the presidency at noon the next day. Released tapes had proved his role in the Watergate cover-up, leaving him facing certain impeachment.</p></div></li></ol>
